human_review:
[staging/src/k8s.io/kubectl/pkg/cmd/create/create.go] I don't think there should be decision logic in the cobra Run func, for a couple of reasons:
1. This breaks from the pattern (most of) the other commands follow.
2. If I am a third party caller using `RunCreate()` and I have `o.EditBeforeCreate = true`, it will silently ignore this option without returning an error, which would be surprising behavior.

What if there is a way to preserve the existing RunCreate interface while accommodating the callers who don't want to construct a cobra command?

```go
func (o *CreateOptions) RunCreate(f cmdutil.Factory, cmd *cobra.Command) error {
	...

	if o.EditBeforeCreate {
        // you can't use EditBeforeCreate if you don't pass in a command!
		if cmd == nil {
			return fmt.Errorf("edit requires a command to be specified")
		}
		return RunEditOnCreate(f, o.PrintFlags, o.RecordFlags, o.IOStreams, cmd, &o.FilenameOptions, o.fieldManager)
	}
    ...
}
```

This works because you've already refactored out ApplyAnnotationsFlag into `Complete()`.

A caller can do `o.RunCreate(f, nil)` if they don't want to construct a cobra command.

What do you think?  Does this satisfy the original issue's needs or is something more explicit needed?

