[pkg/volume/util/operationexecutor/operation_executor_test.go] Rather than baking in an assumption on the number of concurrent routines, which may break in the future and be hard to maintain, why not time out the operation start? That seems more in line with the general assumption anyway.

```
func startOperationAndBlock(ch chan<- interface{}, quit <-chan interface{}) {                                                                                  
    select {
      case ch <- nil:
      case time.After(10*time.Second):
         // probably this will be ignored but at least it gives us a fighting chance in the future if
         // a race is introduced.
         log.Warning("possible race condition: started operation not checked in test")
    }                                                                                                                                                  
    <-quit                                                                                                                                                     
}   
```

Generally I feel that solving concurrency problems by adding buffering to a channel is an anti-pattern.

