[pkg/kubelet/cm/memorymanager/policy_static.go] ```go
if !p.nodeHasCPUs(nodeID) && numaState.NumberOfAssignments == 0 {
	continue
}
```
This is “no CPUs and no existing allocations” condition. If a CPU-less node already has NumberOfAssignments > 0, it is kept.

[pkg/kubelet/cm/memorymanager/policy_static.go] Let's drop this function altogether, and instead implement `selectableNUMANodes` above as:
```
func (p *staticPolicy) selectableNUMANodes(machineState state.NUMANodeMap) []int {
	var numaNodes []int
	for nodeID := range machineState {
		if !p.numaNodesWithCPUs.Has(nodeID) {
			continue
		}
		numaNodes = append(numaNodes, nodeID)
	}
	sort.Ints(numaNodes)
	return numaNodes
}
```

