[pkg/kubelet/cm/topologymanager/helpers.go] OK, second look. This is not really about QOS but rather about a container **wanting** to have exclusive resources, which we determine from resource requests. I think the closest example is actually my old (and stuck for reasons unclear :\) https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/128728.

This function should split in 2 parts, one for cpumanager and one for memory manager and renamed like `ContainerCanHaveExclusiveResource` and should be moved in the specific resource manager.

The container manager can just `logical or` the per-manager check, like in
```
func (cm *containerManagerImpl) CanAllocateExclusively(res v1.ResourceName) bool {
	// run from the cheapest to the most expensive
	return cm.cpuManager.CanAllocateExclusively(res) || cm.memoryManager.CanAllocateExclusively(res) || cm.deviceManager.CanAllocateExclusively(res)
}
```

All of the above should devolve in some trivial rename and trivial code movement and should not be a big deal.

