human_review:
[staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/runtime/helper.go] Couple more thoughts:
1. I think (1) from above is still something I don't have any reasonable answer.
2. Regaring Jordan`s suggestion about the interface for `CacheableObject`, I'm now leaning toward the interface to be more like:
```
type CacheableObject interface {
  // The assumption is that for a given identifier we assume that if called multiple times, 
  // encode function will always be the same.
  CacheEncode(id SerializerIdentifier, encode func(runtime.Object, io.Writer)) ([]byte, error)
  // Probably also
  GetObject(id SerializerIdentifier) runtime.Object
```

The first makes it easy to use, because we simply pass some identifier, and encoder.Encode() function as parameters.
The second (in some form) will probably be needed to handle places like https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/endpoints/handlers/response.go#L40 (it seems that currently this is the only place, but who knows how it will look like in the future).

