[staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/filters/priority-and-fairness.go] is `defer utilruntime.HandleCrash()` enough here? If the `handler.ServeHTTP(w, innerReq)` panics inside this goroutine then we need to propagate the panic to the caller goroutine, so `WithPanicRecovery` can do the proper accounting. 

It's similar to how we have timeout filter today: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/filters/timeout.go#L94-L108

```
	go func() {
		defer func() {
			err := recover()
			// do not wrap the sentinel ErrAbortHandler panic value
			if err != nil && err != http.ErrAbortHandler {
				// Same as stdlib http server code. Manually allocate stack
				// trace buffer size to prevent excessively large logs
				const size = 64 << 10
				buf := make([]byte, size)
				buf = buf[:runtime.Stack(buf, false)]
				err = fmt.Sprintf("%v\n%s", err, buf)
			}
			resultCh <- err
		}()
		t.handler.ServeHTTP(tw, r)
	}()
```

I am not fully aware of how differently we handle a `Watch` than a regular request, but `WithPanicRecovery` seems to apply to all requests, I believe.

[staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/filters/priority-and-fairness.go] > What I'm wondering about is what this doesn't cause any test failures.
Isn't the context actually eventually closed when the request is processed (the same way as for regular requests)?

what may be happening here is that `ctx.Done() == nil` for `Watch` since we are not setting any deadline for long running and watch requests. (`WithRequestDeadline` only sets deadline to non long running requests).
the goroutine is spun up only when `ctx.Done() ` is non nil, see the code snippets from `StartRequest`
```
        doneCh := ctx.Done()
	if doneCh != nil {
		qs.preCreateOrUnblockGoroutine()
		go func() {
			defer runtime.HandleCrash()
			qs.goroutineDoneOrBlocked()
			_ = <-doneCh
			// Whatever goroutine unblocked the preceding receive MUST
			// have already either (a) incremented qs.counter or (b)
			// known that said counter is not actually counting or (c)
			// known that the count does not need to be accurate.
			// BTW, the count only needs to be accurate in a test that
			// uses FakeEventClock::Run().
			klog.V(6).Infof("QS(%s): Context of request %q %#+v %#+v is Done", configName, fsName, descr1, descr2)
			qs.cancelWait(req)
			qs.goroutineDoneOrBlocked()
		}()
	}
```
so we may not even be creating the goroutine at all for `Watch`.

