[staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/storage/cacher/cacher_whitebox_test.go] I was looking at the `TestGetListNonRecursiveCacheBypass` and here is what I have seen:

```
func TestGetListNonRecursiveCacheBypass(t *testing.T) {
	...
	cacher, _, err := newTestCacher(backingStorage)
	...
	if !utilfeature.DefaultFeatureGate.Enabled(features.ResilientWatchCacheInitialization) {
		if err := cacher.ready.wait(context.Background()); err != nil {
			t.Fatalf("unexpected error waiting for the cache to be ready")
		}
	}
```

after checking `newTestCacher` i realised that this method will wait for the cacher to be ready as well:

```
if utilfeature.DefaultFeatureGate.Enabled(features.ResilientWatchCacheInitialization) {
		// The tests assume that Get/GetList/Watch calls shouldn't fail.
		// However, 429 error can now be returned if watchcache is under initialization.
		// To avoid rewriting all tests, we wait for watcache to initialize.
		if err := cacher.ready.wait(context.Background()); err != nil {
			return nil, storage.APIObjectVersioner{}, err
		}
	}
```

So it seems that regardless of whether the feature is enabled or disabled the tests will wait for the cacher to be ready.

