[pkg/kubelet/pleg/generic.go] Unlike `podsToReinspect`, `podNeedsReSync` is triggered by the `doPodResizeAction` function in `SyncPod` and generates an independent `PodSync` event. This distinguishes it from regular container events, thus ensuring that even when no container events occur, it can trigger a new container event to drive `SyncPod` and maintain consistency.

Ideally, the `podNeedsReSync` mechanism already has a reinspection characteristic. Only after the cache is correctly updated and `g.completePodReSync(pid)` is called will it stop generating events in subsequent listing cycles. Otherwise, it will continue to trigger reinspection.
```
			select {
			case g.eventChannel <- events[i]:
				// After successfully triggering the syncPod event,
				// we won’t trigger it again at the next Relist. If the channel is full,
				// we will trigger it again at the next Relist.
				if events[i].Type == PodSync {
					g.completePodReSync(pid)
				}
```

