[pkg/controller/resourceclaim/controller.go] Discussed on slack, after this PR, the annotation is being used by drivers to determine the pod claim name from the resource claim object it has available.

This feature assumes that consumers like kubevirt virt-launcher pod, which does not have access to kubernetes API will not be able to get pod status information. Since pod status is not available, these consumers will not able to look at the resource claim name from the template in the spec. Hence they need the annotation here as a formal API to look up the claim name. I have updated the doc.go to reflect this. Also, as a follow-up, the KEP needs this update as well.

```
// The directory layout distinguishes between two kinds of claims because
// consumers may only have access to the pod spec (e.g., when running
// without access to the Kubernetes API) 
```

Without kubernetes API, kubevirt virt-launcher pod has access to its own CRD Spec, which gets converted to pod spec, hence we can assume access to pod spec to read and discover the metadata

